$$F_C(x) = x + \sum_{C_1} x^{\operatorname{comp}(C_1)+1} F_{C_1}(x) + \sum_{C_1,C_2} x^{\operatorname{comp}(C_2)+\operatorname{comp}(C_1)+1} F_{C_2}(x)F_{C_1}(x) + \cdots$$

At each level, prepending a set $C_i$ to the left of the type tree adds $\operatorname{comp}(C_i)$ to the exponent. After full expansion:

$$F_C(x) = x + x\sum_{k \geq 1}\left(\sum_S x^{\operatorname{comp}(S)} F_S(x)\right)^k$$

Define $P(x) = \sum_S x^{\operatorname{comp}(S)} F_S(x)$. Then:

$$F_C(x) = x + x\cdot\frac{P(x)}{1-P(x)} = \frac{x}{1-P(x)}$$

## Universal Formula

The same expansion works for **any** set $T$ with $\operatorname{comp}(T)=t$:

$$F_T(x) = \frac{x^t}{1-P(x)}$$

